ssic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1446469-new-dev-blog-by-justin-achilli?p=1446540#post1446540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can believe some Sabbat would do that, or at least some young and stupid ones that could be talked into such action. I doubt they would survive long enough to make a Path.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Church of Caine does something like that:<br /> <br /> &quot;Willpower is all-important to these vampires, who believe that in order to emulate (or even surpass) Caine, one must harden one\u2019s mind against hell\u2019s weaponry. Gnostics are expected to sample a snatch of sunlight, walk through fire, and adorn themselves with holy symbols, just to show their defiance and power.&quot;<br /> <br /> It reminds me of the Mystery of the Ascendant in VtR:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Mystery of the Ascendant follows one strict doctrine: The sun is the enemy; to overcome its rays is to overcome all adversity.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's bit different, because the Mysterious of the Dragon enable vampires to ultimately accomplish things like resistance to sunlight, so it's a constructive pursuit, and because they see it as a way to defy God rather than getting closer to him. It wouldn't be enough for a whole path, but perhaps there could be a path based around the idea that vampires are great <i>if</i> they can overcome their unique weaknesses. High blood potency may also be an aspiration for them, even for thin-bloods.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":